<template>
    <children>
        <li id="29.lp5"/>
        <li id="20.lp5"/>
        <li id="31.lp5"/>
        <li id="21.lp5"/>
        <li id="26.lp5"/>
    </children>
    <heading>JavaScript units</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>JavaScript</li>
        <li>units</li>
        <li>model</li>
        <li>controller</li>
        <li>operations</li>
        <li>view</li>
        <li>utility</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>Unit boundaries separate responsibilities that change for different reasons: the model owns project data, storage supplies file access, the view owns mounted UI, and operations decide which commands may act on them. The controller supplies the call/return mechanism without knowing project-specific states. Utilities provide shared mechanisms without selecting application policy.</p>
        <p>Definitions share the enclosing application scope, so units can cooperate without making every helper public. Public members of <code>window.LP5</code> form the interface used by template scripts and startup.</p>
    </section>
</template>
